From d0d0124c16832703b6bc6743c0f0a48ec8d1d654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chronium <chronium@interlink.local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:48:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] chronium: render-time noise v2, per-context WebGL
 extensions, audio fix

Engine Fix Notes (leak test 15/09/2026) A1, A2, A6, A7.

noise.version (new, default 1). Version 1 keeps the legacy read-time
canvas noise so profiles already signed in keep their hashes. Version 2
perturbs at render time and never on read:
- A6: canvas text is drawn with a seeded 0.25-0.45 px horizontal shift
  and 0.15-0.4% scale about its anchor
  (BaseRenderingContext2D::DrawTextInternal, shared by OffscreenCanvas).
  Chrome 148 snaps glyphs to quarter pixels horizontally, so the shift
  always changes short strings and emoji; the scale varies long strings.
  Flat fills and putImageData round-trips stay exact, and getImageData,
  toDataURL and toBlob read the same bitmap. Legacy LSB noise in
  getImageData / toDataURL / toBlob is off in version 2.
- A1: vertex shaders get a seeded 2e-4..6e-4 clip-space offset on
  gl_Position.xy (shaderSource rewrite: #define main + #line + appended
  wrapper; getShaderSource returns the original). readPixels, toDataURL
  and drawImage agree; a clear or flat quad is untouched. #line keeps
  compile-error line numbers (checked on ANGLE, ESSL 1.00 and 3.00).
- noise.canvas_threshold = 0 now turns canvas noise off (both schemes);
  noise.webgl_readpixels toggles the WebGL noise.

A7: getSupportedExtensions() filters the real list through a per-context
allowlist (webgl.extensions for WebGL2, new webgl.extensions_webgl1 for
WebGL1; no list = real list), and getExtension() applies the same
allowlist, so listed == resolvable on both context types.

A2: audio noise moved from read time (AudioBuffer::getChannelData) to a
single pass in OfflineAudioContext::FireCompletionEvent, so
getChannelData == copyFromChannel and script-written buffers (CreepJS
trap) stay exact. noise.audio_amplitude is now the real amplitude
(clamped to [0, 1e-2]); AnalyserNode readouts scale with it and leave
silence untouched.

New switches: --fingerprint-webgl1-extensions, --fingerprint-noise-version,
--fingerprint-canvas-noise, --fingerprint-webgl-readpixels-noise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
